From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:27:48 +0200
Subject: Game controllers: Walnut's standard scheme, second bindings, hot-plug
 scan

A pad's default bindings (GamepadConfig::initSDLMapping, used when a pad
has no saved configuration) are now one fixed scheme in the SDL game
controller names, for a DualShock 3 and any pad with the usual buttons:

  R2 / R1            accelerate         L2 / L1        brake / reverse
  left stick, d-pad  steer              Cross (A)      skid
  Square (X)         fire the item      Circle (B)     nitro
  Triangle (Y)       look back          Select (Back)  rescue
  Start              pause

  menus: left stick or d-pad move, Cross (or Start) select, Circle back.

An action can now have a second binding (DeviceConfig::setAltBinding,
saved in input.xml as a second <action ... alt="true"> and listed as
"R2 / R1" in Options > Input): the trigger and the shoulder button, the
stick and the d-pad. Setting a binding by hand clears the second one.
The keyboard keeps working at the same time (its own device).

Hot-plug: SDL's added event could be lost or the open could fail at that
moment, and a pad plugged in later was not found. InputManager::update
now also looks every 2 s for a pad SDL lists that is not open, and the
added event ignores one already open.

A pad that already has a saved configuration in input.xml keeps it.

